Subject: Astral Form?
Lines: 42

I had a weird idea for a spell yesterday.  WIBNI (Wouldn't it be neat if)
you could temporarily leave your body, and have your spirit explore the
level?

Advantages:
   You could find all the traps without getting caught by them
      (slightly better than levitation in this regard)
   You can pass through walls (like ghosts and xorns)
   You don't have to worry about the monsters, since you're not
      really there.  I guess either you couldn't move onto a square with
      a monster, or you'd have to 'push' it aside like you do your pet.

DisAdvantages
   You can't fight things while in astral form
   Your body may still be susceptible to attack while you are
      wandering (although it won't be scuffing up Elbereth at all)
   If your body actually Is attacked (esp by thrown weapons),
      you have to move your astral form back across the level to
      reanimate it (i.e. don't wander off Too far)
   Your astral form may still be susceptible to Mind Flayers

Implementation ideas
   I think this would work best as a spell from a spellbook,
   probably of very high level.  Its duration would be indefinite.
   I know there's already the ability to 'clone' yourself
   (since it is done with gremlins).  So you'd leave your clone
   behind, and then move yourself around, with an 'astral'
   property bit set on.

   Of course, it would be a pain to modify everything that says
   that astral forms can't pick things up, or attack, or drink
   from fountains, etc.

Sound cool?

